    "title": "Japan Thinks About the Unthinkable: Nuclear Arms",
    "text": "For decades, Japan has relied on the U.S. nuclear umbrella—Washington's promise to defend its allies, including with nuclear weapons.\nBut now, some are starting to consider the unthinkable: for the only country to have ever suffered an atomic bomb attack, Japan may need to acquire weapons of mass destruction itself. This shift is linked to rising threats from China and North Korea.",
